+/* Every colour target of at most PS3RECOMP_ENG_WB_SMALL pixels (default 1024;
+ * 0 turns it off) goes back to guest memory at every frame end. A title can
+ * read a small GPU result straight out of VRAM with the CPU -- inFAMOUS 2
+ * reads its 20x11 average-luminance reduction for auto-exposure -- and
+ * nothing else would write it back: the frame came out at half its
+ * brightness. Recorded before the present, so it rides in the frame's own
+ * batch; a backend with readback_deferred hands the rows over when that batch
