+#   - ppu_mm_take reads a per-unit cache filled once (the globals it copies are
+#     all set before any guest code runs: vm_base, ppu_vm_size, vm_inline_ok and
+#     vm_inline_st_ok, ppu_hle_inject_base) instead of recomputing the span with
+#     a dozen instructions at every function entry;
+#   - a store tests the runtime's reservation bitmap array (g_spu_coh_bitmap,
+#     all zero until an SPU reserves a line) directly, before and after it
+#     lands: no pointer load, no NULL test;
+#   - a store no longer tests g_barrier_sync_watch | g_null_sweep_hi: the probes
+#     behind them (SPU_ATOM_EA, PS3_NULL_SWEEP) clear vm_inline_ok, so the span
+#     is 0 and every store already takes the out-of-line path that runs them;
+#   - the out-of-line accesses go through register-preserving thunks (see the
+#     block), lvx/stvx through the copy as one 16-byte access, and the source
+#     preamble gets the trampoline drain out of line (FAST_MM_SOURCE);
+#   - stvx's locked slow path takes a copy of the source, so a vector register
+#     held in a local (--local-vrs) does not escape into a call.
